#: src/mailman/bin/runner.py:76
msgid ""
"    Start a runner.\n"
"\n"
"    The runner named on the command line is started, and it can either run\n"
"    through its main loop once (for those runners that support this) or\n"
"    continuously.  The latter is how the master runner starts all its\n"
"    subprocesses.\n"
"\n"
"    -r is required unless -l or -h is given, and its argument must be one of\n"
"    the names displayed by the -l switch.\n"
"\n"
"    Normally, this script should be started from `mailman start`.  Running it\n"
"    separately or with -o is generally useful only for debugging.  When run\n"
"    this way, the environment variable $MAILMAN_UNDER_MASTER_CONTROL will be\n"
"    set which subtly changes some error handling behavior.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    Mulai sebuah runner.\n"
"\n"
"    Runner yang dinamai pada baris perintah akan dijalankan, dan dapat "
"dijalankan\n"
"    melalui loop utamanya satu kali (untuk runner yang mendukung ini) atau\n"
"    terus-menerus. Cara kedua inilah yang digunakan runner master untuk "
"memulai semua\n"
"    subprosesnya.\n"
"\n"
"    -r wajib diberikan kecuali jika -l atau -h digunakan, dan argumennya "
"harus salah satu\n"
"    nama yang ditampilkan oleh opsi -l.\n"
"\n"
"    Biasanya, skrip ini harus dijalankan dari `mailman start`. "
"Menjalankannya\n"
"    secara terpisah atau dengan -o umumnya hanya berguna untuk debugging. "
"Jika dijalankan\n"
"    dengan cara ini, variabel lingkungan $MAILMAN_UNDER_MASTER_CONTROL akan\n"
"    diatur, yang sedikit mengubah beberapa perilaku penanganan kesalahan.\n"
"    "

#: src/mailman/bin/runner.py:103
msgid "List the available runner names and exit."
msgstr "Daftar nama runner yang tersedia lalu keluar."

#: src/mailman/bin/runner.py:107
msgid ""
"    Run the named runner exactly once through its main loop.  Otherwise, the\n"
"    runner runs indefinitely until the process receives a signal.  This is not\n"
"    compatible with runners that cannot be run once."
msgstr ""
"    Jalankan runner yang dinamai tepat satu kali melalui loop utamanya. Jika "
"tidak,\n"
"    runner berjalan tanpa batas sampai proses menerima sinyal. Ini tidak\n"
"    kompatibel dengan runner yang tidak dapat dijalankan satu kali."

#: src/mailman/bin/runner.py:115
msgid ""
"\n"
"    Start the named runner, which must be one of the strings returned by the -l\n"
"    option.\n"
"\n"
"    For runners that manage a queue directory, optional `slice:range` if given\n"
"    is used to assign multiple runner processes to that queue.  range is the\n"
"    total number of runners for the queue while slice is the number of this\n"
"    runner from [0..range).  For runners that do not manage a queue, slice and\n"
"    range are ignored.\n"
"\n"
"    When using the `slice:range` form, you must ensure that each runner for the\n"
"    queue is given the same range value.  If `slice:runner` is not given, then\n"
"    1:1 is used.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"    Mulai runner yang dinamai, yang harus merupakan salah satu string yang "
"dikembalikan oleh opsi -l.\n"
"\n"
"    Untuk runner yang mengelola direktori antrean, `slice:range` opsional "
"jika diberikan\n"
"    digunakan untuk menetapkan beberapa proses runner ke antrean tersebut. "
"range adalah\n"
"    jumlah total runner untuk antrean, sedangkan slice adalah nomor runner "
"ini\n"
"    dari [0..range). Untuk runner yang tidak mengelola antrean, slice dan\n"
"    range diabaikan.\n"
"\n"
"    Saat menggunakan bentuk `slice:range`, Anda harus memastikan bahwa "
"setiap runner untuk\n"
"    antrean diberi nilai range yang sama. Jika `slice:runner` tidak "
"diberikan, maka\n"
"    1:1 digunakan.\n"
"    "

